  "body": "`[[error]]` clears `[[queue]]` and synchronously puts the `ReadableStream` into the `\"errored\"` state. I wonder if there's use cases of error-after-drain, that is error delivered to the public API side after all queued data is read out like how close() is delivered.\n\nOne thing I come up with is receiving data from network, fail due to network issue, and then resume receiving. It's not good to throw away correctly received data remaining in the `[[queue]]`.\n",
